Short:        Zune GUI toolkit for classic AmigaOS
Author:       The AROS Development Team and contributors
Uploader:     Stefan Reinauer <stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org>
Type:         util/libs
Version:      [RELEASE] - [STAGE]
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.1+, 68000+, Installer 43+

Zune68 is a native AmigaOS 3 port of the current AROS Zune GUI toolkit.
It aims to improve compatibility with classic MUI applications while
keeping CPU and memory costs practical on ordinary 68000-based Amigas.

This release ([STAGE], [RELEASE]) contains muimaster.library [VERSION]
and the side-by-side zunemaster.library, the Zune preferences editor,
[PLUGINS] optional MUI class plugins, translations, SDK headers, examples
and corresponding source. The library reports the version of MUI 5,
because applications enable their current code paths by it; Zune68
releases are identified by their date.
The native code builds with m68k-amigaos-gcc and requires no FPU.

Use the supplied Amiga Installer script. It installs every component,
saves each file it replaces, and asks only before replacing a newer
third-party class.
Classes go to MUI:Libs/MUI; without MUI:, the installer assigns it.
Installing muimaster.library changes the toolkit used by MUI applications.
Every run is logged in MUI:Zune68/Install.log, and running the installer
again offers Set back, which returns to the MUI setup from before Zune68.
The plugins are loaded only when requested.

IBrowse 3.1 and 3.0a, YAM 2.x, Voyager 3.5.2, Odyssey Web Browser, AmiPG and
XSysInfo run; IBrowse is pretty usable.

This is a beta: there are many ways Zune68 can still improve, and broad
MUI application coverage needs real-world use. We need testers. Please try
your MUI applications with Zune68 and report what works and what doesn't.
See ReadMe and Compatibility for details.

Project: https://github.com/reinauer/zune68
